  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "أَحْمَدُ بْنُ مُحَمَّدٍ عَنْ عَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحَكَمِ عَنْ سَيْفٍ عَنْ عَمْرَو بْنِ شِمْرٍ عَنْ جَابِرٍ عَنْ أَبِي جَعْفَرٍ ع قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated from Ali ibn al-Hakam from Saif from 'Amr ibn Shimir from Jabir from Abu Ja'far (peace be upon him) who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ الْمُكَاتَبِ يُشْتَرَطُ عَلَيْهِ إِنْ عَجَزَ فَهُوَ رَدٌّ فِي الرِّقِّ، فَعَجَزَ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُؤَدِّيَ شَيْئًا فَقَالَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ ع لَا تَرُدُّهُ فِي الرِّقِّ حَتَّى تَمضيَ لَهُ ثَلَاثُ سِنِينَ وَيَعْتِقَ مِنْهُ بِمِقْدَارِ مَا أَدَّى، فَأَمَّا إِذَا صَبَرُوا فَلَيْسَ لَهُمْ أَنْ يَرُدُّوا فِي الرِّقِّ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "I asked him about the mukatab (a slave who has contracted to pay a sum for his freedom) upon whom it is stipulated that if he becomes unable to pay, he returns to slavery. He became unable before paying anything. He (Abu Ja'far, peace be upon him) said: Do not return him to slavery until three years have passed for him, and he is freed from the remainder by the amount he has paid. As for if they (the master) are patient, it is not for them to return him to slavery."
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith outlines the legal ruling for a mukatab (slave with a manumission contract) who fails to pay the agreed sum due to inability (ajz). Imam al-Baqir (peace be upon him) rules that the master cannot immediately re-enslave the slave but must wait three years, during which the slave is partially freed proportional to what he has paid. If the master remains patient during this period, he forfeits the right to re-enslave the slave.",
      "seo_question": "What is the ruling for a slave who cannot pay his manumission debt (mukatab) before paying anything?",
